From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 13:31:18 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Tick chosen worlds on their own threads

A world given its own thread (Athena.startWorldThread) is ticked there every
50 ms by AthenaWorldThread with the same per-world tick the server thread runs
for the others (MinecraftServer.athenaTickWorld), so a stall in it holds up that
world alone and a stall on the server thread leaves it ticking. The world's
postToMainThread and isMainThread answer for its thread, AsyncCatcher checks
work on one world against that world's thread, and timers that counted
MinecraftServer.currentTick count the world's own tick (World.athenaCurrentTick,
which is currentTick for the worlds the server thread ticks). The server thread
stops a world's thread before unloading it and at shutdown, and autosaves it
there. Timings are turned off when the first world thread starts.

Not for players yet: a world with players cannot get its own thread, players
cannot be teleported into one, entities cannot change worlds into or out of one,
and chunk preloads refuse one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

